Fix #1321

If user want to turn `Result<T, unknown>` into `Result<T, E>`, then user should use `mapErr()` for it. For example, 

```ts
const produced: Result<string, unknown> = tryCatchIntoResult(() => {
    return createSomething(blahblah);
});
const result: Result<string, Error> = mapErrForResult(produced, (e: unknown) => {
    if (e instanceof Error) {
        return e;
    }
    return new Error('....', { cause: e });
});
```
